  "body": "### Description\r\n\r\nI am on the way to migrate from a shared synapse installation to my own. I noticed that on my own server (server B) I see less members in rooms that on the shared one (A). In one room, I only see one less (28) on server B than on server A (29). That person can't see my messages in the room, and I can't see theirs.\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n- Join `#synapse:matrix.org` from server A: 2885 members, topic includes `Current release: 1.49.2`\r\n- Join `#synapse:matrix.org` from server B: 2117 members, topic includes `Current release: 1.49.0`\r\n\r\nI'd love to supply more details from the logs but I don't really know what to search for since the logs are huge, especially after joining the synapse admins room. I already tried to get support in `#synapse:matrix.org` but didn't get feedback.\r\n\r\n### Version information (server B)\r\n\r\n- **Homeserver**: varac.net (https://federationtester.matrix.org/#varac.net)\r\n- **Version**: 1.49.2\r\n- **Install method**: Kubernetes (k3s v1.21.5+k3s2), [synapse helm char](thttps://artifacthub.io/packages/helm/halkeye/synapse) v1.49.0\r\n- **Platform**: Selfhosted Ganeti VM (kvm), Debian buster\r\n",
